---
import Highlight from '../components/Highlight.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Sponsor an issue · The Lazy Horseman"
  description="Sponsor one issue of The Lazy Horseman: one honest, clearly marked slot for useful equestrian products and services."
>
  <section class="band cream-band page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">One per issue, never more</p>
      <h1>Sponsor an <Highlight>issue</Highlight></h1>
      <p class="lede">The letter exists to check whether things are true. That puts a limit on who can sensibly pay to sit next to it, so it is worth being straight about who fits.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band cream-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="prose" style="margin-bottom:18px">Who tends to fit</h2>
      <div class="fitlist">
        <div class="fit w1"><h3>People who make the kit</h3><p>Rugs, boots, haynets, hard feed, supplements, fencing, trailers. Anything a reader already owns three of and has opinions about.</p></div>
        <div class="fit w2"><h3>People who turn up at the yard</h3><p>Farriers, physios, saddle fitters, dentists, trainers, transport. Especially regional ones, because readers want to know who is any good near them.</p></div>
        <div class="fit w3"><h3>Yards and services</h3><p>Livery yards taking bookings, arenas, insurers, competition centres, and anyone building something useful for horse people.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="notfit">
        <h3>And who does not</h3>
        <p>Anything sold on a claim it cannot back up. If the product needs the words miracle, detox, or secret to make sense, we are going to have an awkward conversation, because sooner or later the letter will take a proper look at it. Sponsors are told this before they pay, not after.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>One sponsor per issue. Your slot sits inside the letter, written in the same voice as everything around it, clearly marked as paid, and never dressed up as something I found on my own. You see the copy before it goes out and you get the final say on it.</p>
        <p>I will not write that I use something when I do not, and I will not recommend a product I have not looked at. That is the whole reason anyone opens the thing on a Thursday, and it is not for sale.</p>
        <p>Tell me what you make or do and roughly when you would want a slot, and I will come back with what is free, what it costs, and the current subscriber figures in writing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band cta-block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Let's talk about it.</h2>
      <p>Opens your email app with the subject line ready. Tell me who you are and what you are after. No deck needed.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="mailto:hello@thelazyhorseman.com?subject=Sponsoring%20an%20issue&amp;body=Who%20we%20are%3A%0A%0AWhat%20we%20make%20or%20do%3A%0A%0ARoughly%20when%20we%27d%20want%20a%20slot%3A%0A%0A">Email about sponsoring</a>
      <p class="cta-note">hello@thelazyhorseman.com, and I answer these myself.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
